# EtAmountInputDisplay Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtAmountInputDisplay` renders a hero monetary amount as a single row - optional leading currency symbol, an animated number (`EtAnimatedCount`), an optional blinking caret, and an optional trailing unit label - and scales the whole row down as one unit so the amount:

- shrinks progressively from ~the 6th digit (so large numbers never look huge), and
- always fits its container width (fit-to-width guard for extreme values),

with currency and unit shrinking in lockstep with the number because the entire row shares one `transform: scale`.

It is the **display surface of an amount-entry flow** (the caret + shake exist because a keypad like `EtNumericKeypad` drives its value), but it is itself display-only: it is fully controlled via `value` and has no `onChange`/keyboard. It exists so consumers do not have to re-implement the `onLayout` measuring + scale wiring that a currency/unit amount needs. The scale engine is the component's own `useAmountAutoScale` hook (in `animations/`); this component owns rendering the affixes and measuring them.

**Relationship to `EtAnimatedCount`:** `EtAnimatedCount` is the digit-rolling *primitive* (number only). `EtAmountInputDisplay` composes it and adds currency/unit affixes, auto-scale, caret, and shake.

**Does NOT handle:** input/editing (display only - caller owns `value`), locale formatting (pass a pre-formatted string), or negative-sign layout.

## Two APIs

### Props (plug and play)

```tsx
<EtAmountInputDisplay value="1,234.56" currencySymbol="$" unitLabel="Shares" showCursor shakeTrigger={rejectCount} />
```

Defaults reproduce the trade execution hero (60px number in `textPrimaryNeutral`, 32px affixes in `textSecondaryNeutral`, `statusPositive` caret), so the props path looks right with zero styling.

### Compound (custom arrangement / per-part styling)

```tsx
<EtAmountInputDisplay value="42">
  <EtAmountInputDisplay.Currency>€</EtAmountInputDisplay.Currency>
  <EtAmountInputDisplay.Value />
  <EtAmountInputDisplay.Caret />
  <EtAmountInputDisplay.Unit>Units</EtAmountInputDisplay.Unit>
</EtAmountInputDisplay>
```

When children are present the props arrangement is ignored. Subcomponents read geometry/colors from context and (currency/unit/caret) report their measured widths back to the root's scale math.

## How the auto-scale works

The root measures the container (`onLayout`) and sums the affix widths reported by the subcomponents into `affixWidth`. That, plus the value's own `EtAnimatedCount` slot geometry, feeds `useAmountAutoScale({ value, availableWidth, affixWidth, digitWidth })`, which returns an animated `scaleStyle`. The tween is 100% UI thread (`useSharedValue` + `withTiming` + `useAnimatedStyle`, transform-only). The target scale is computed on JS because its inputs (measured widths + value) originate as JS-thread state.

This is why the shrink lives here and not inside `EtAnimatedCount`: the number component only holds digits, whereas the shrink must include the currency/unit affixes, so it belongs at the row that renders them.

## Key props

| Prop | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `value` | required | Formatted string that drives the number and the scale. |
| `currencySymbol` / `unitLabel` | - | Props-path affixes. |
| `showCursor` | false | Blinking caret after the number. |
| `shakeTrigger` | 0 | Monotonic counter; each increment plays an error shake + haptic. |
| `autoScale` | true | Set false to disable both progressive + overflow shrink. |
| `fontSize` / `digitWidth` / `digitHeight` / `affixFontSize` / `currencyFontSize` | 60 / 35 / 72 / 32 / 40 | Geometry (also feeds the scale math). Currency runs larger than the unit affix. |
| `numberColor` / `affixColor` / `currencyColor` / `caretColor` | theme (`textPrimaryNeutral` / `textSecondaryNeutral` / `carbon300` / `statusPositive`) | Color overrides. |
| `shrinkStartDigits` / `shrinkStepPerDigit` / `progressiveMinScale` / `overflowMinScale` | 5 / 0.08 / 0.5 / 0.3 | Scale-curve tuning (passthrough to `useAmountAutoScale`). |

## Dependencies

- Own `animations/` folder: `useAmountInputDisplayAnimations` (orchestrator) composing `useAmountAutoScale`, `useShakeAnimation`, `useCaretBlinkAnimation`; pure scale math in `utils/` (`computeAmountScale`, `getAnimatedCountWidth`).
- `EtAnimatedCount` (foundations/animated-digits), `EtText` (foundations/text).
- `useEtoroTheme` for default colors.

## Testing

Mock the heavy leaf `../../../foundations/animated-digits` (`EtAnimatedCount` -> a `<Text testID="amount-input-display-count">`) and `expo-haptics`. `useEtoroTheme` is auto-mocked by the ui test setup. Stable testIDs: `amount-input-display-container`, `amount-input-display-row`, `amount-input-display-currency`, `amount-input-display-unit`, `amount-input-display-caret`, `amount-input-display-count`.

## File Map

Structured after the canonical `components/button` role model (see `building-ui-components.mdc`):
`animations/` owns every animated style/builder, `hooks/` is logic-only, and the context is split by
update frequency so affixes don't re-render on every keystroke.

```
amount-input-display/
├── api/
│   ├── index.ts
│   └── types.ts                                 # EtAmountInputDisplayProps, AmountInputDisplayAffixProps
├── animations/
│   ├── constants.ts                             # makeRoomTransition, caret/shake/settle constants
│   ├── use-amount-input-display-animations.ts   # orchestrator: auto-scale + shake + caret -> styles + caretOpacity
│   ├── use-amount-auto-scale.ts                 # fit-to-width + progressive scale (UI thread)
│   ├── use-caret-blink-animation.ts             # blinking caret opacity
│   ├── use-shake-animation.ts                   # error shake translateX + haptic
│   └── index.ts
├── context/                                     # split by update frequency
│   ├── config-context.tsx                       # static geometry/colors
│   ├── state-context.tsx                        # caretOpacity + affix-width registry callbacks
│   ├── value-context.tsx                        # hot path: the value string
│   ├── amount-input-display-provider.tsx        # composed provider
│   └── index.ts
├── hooks/
│   ├── index.ts
│   ├── use-amount-input-display-config.ts       # props + theme -> resolved geometry/colors (memoized)
│   └── use-amount-input-display-state.ts        # affix-width registry + availableWidth (logic-only)
├── subcomponents/
│   ├── amount-input-display-currency.tsx        # EtAmountInputDisplay.Currency (measures + reports width)
│   ├── amount-input-display-value.tsx           # EtAmountInputDisplay.Value -> EtAnimatedCount
│   ├── amount-input-display-caret.tsx           # EtAmountInputDisplay.Caret (blink + reserved width)
│   ├── amount-input-display-unit.tsx            # EtAmountInputDisplay.Unit (measures + reports width)
│   └── index.ts
├── utils/                                       # pure: compute-amount-scale, get-animated-count-width (+ specs)
├── constants.ts                                 # non-animation defaults (font size, digit geometry)
├── styles.ts
├── et-amount-input-display.tsx                  # composition (props path + compound children)
├── index.ts
├── tests/et-amount-input-display.test.tsx
└── AGENTS.mdc
```
